// ---- render the CV library into the (static, cacheable) system prompt ----
const CV_BLOCK = Object.entries(CV_LIBRARY).map(([id, cv]) =>
`### CV OPTION: ${id}
Label: ${cv.label}
Typically used for: ${cv.targets.join(', ')}

${cv.text}`).join('\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\n');

const SYSTEM = `You help one candidate triage job ads in ${CFG.country}. You do two things for each ad:
pick which of his CVs fits it best, and judge how good that fit actually is.

He keeps ${Object.keys(CV_LIBRARY).length} tailored CVs. They describe the same career, rewritten for different
target roles — so the choice is about which framing a hiring manager for THIS ad should see.

${CV_BLOCK}

────────────────────────────────────────

WHAT HE IS LOOKING FOR
${CFG.targets}
Based in ${CFG.home_city}; ${CFG.relocation_open ? `open to relocating within ${CFG.country}` : `not willing to relocate`}. Salary ${CFG.salary_target}+ is a plus.

HOW TO CHOOSE A CV
Read the ad's actual responsibilities, not just its title — titles are inconsistent across
German job boards. Pick the CV whose experience and framing a hiring manager for this ad
would find most convincing. If none of them is a reasonable fit, still name the closest one
and set new_cv_needed to true.

HOW TO SCORE THE MATCH (cv_match_score, 0-100)
Judge only how well the CHOSEN CV matches this ad's stated requirements: tools, domain,
and the kind of work. Ignore location, language and the years-of-experience requirement
entirely — all three are scored separately downstream, so do not let them move this number.
 - 85-100: strong match. The CV reads like it was written for this ad.
 - 70-84 : good match. Clear overlap on the core asks, minor gaps.
 - 50-69 : partial. Right family of work, but real gaps or a seniority mismatch.
 - 30-49 : weak. Adjacent field, most requirements unmet.
 - 0-29  : wrong role.
Use the full range. If the ad body is empty or near-empty, score on the title alone,
cap at 60, and say so in cv_match_reason.

OPTIONAL -- ADD YOUR OWN HARD-GAP RULES HERE.
The original template had two rules at this spot: a penalty when an ad
required people-management experience the candidate didn't have, and a
penalty when an ad required a specific degree the candidate didn't hold.
Both were specific to that one person and have been removed.

If there's a requirement you know you don't meet (a specific certificate,
years of experience, a degree, a language, a work permit, etc.), you can
describe a similar rule here in plain English and the AI will apply it
consistently. If you don't have anything like that, just delete this
paragraph.

FACTS TO EXTRACT
Report what the ad says, not what you infer, except where noted.
 - city: the work location as a plain city name. "" if the ad does not say.
 - work_mode: "remote" only if the ad says fully/100% remote. "hybrid" if it mixes office
   and home. "onsite" otherwise, including when unstated.
 - de_level / en_level: read the qualifier attached to EACH language SEPARATELY, then
   place each on this ladder (these are the exact words found in real German ads):
     "native"     muttersprachlich, Muttersprache, native speaker
     "fluent"     verhandlungssicher, fliessend, fluent, hervorragend, exzellent,
                  ausgezeichnet, business fluent, or an explicit C1 / C2
     "very_good"  sehr gut, very good, fortgeschritten, advanced, sicher, strong
     "good"       gut, good, solide, solid, professional
     "basic"      Grundkenntnisse, grundlegend, basic, conversational
     "mentioned"  the language IS named as needed/expected, but with NO qualifier at all
                  ("Deutsch und Englisch", "Sprachkenntnisse: Deutsch")
     "none"       the language is not asked for anywhere in the ad
   RULES — these matter more than the ladder itself:
     * A qualifier that belongs to ENGLISH never sets de_level. "Sehr gute Englischkenntnisse
       (C1)" is en_level="fluent", de_level="none". "Projektsprache: Englisch" is the same.
     * If ONE phrase covers both languages ("sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse",
       "fliessend Deutsch und Englisch"), give BOTH languages that level.
     * "Deutschlandticket", "Deutschland", place names and benefits are NOT language asks.
     * DO NOT INFER — this is the single most common mistake. If the ad is merely WRITTEN
       in German but never qualifies German proficiency, de_level is "none"; record that the
       ad is German in ad_language instead. Never read the ad's own language as a requirement.
     * "mentioned" requires the ad to actually NAME German as needed, just without a qualifier.
 - ad_language: "de" or "en" — which language the job ad itself is predominantly written in.
 - required_years: the minimum years of professional experience the ad asks for, as an
   integer. Take the lower bound of a range ("3-5 Jahre Erfahrung" -> 3, "mindestens 5
   Jahre" -> 5). Most German ads name no number but describe the level in words — in that
   case map the wording, because "no number" is not the same as "no requirement":
     "erste Erfahrung", "Berufseinstieg", "Praktikum/Werkstudent", Junior in the title  -> 1
     "einschlaegige Berufserfahrung", "mehrjaehrige Erfahrung", "Berufserfahrung"        -> 3
     "fundierte", "langjaehrige", "umfassende", "nachweisliche" Erfahrung                -> 5
     "Senior", "Lead", "Principal", "Head of" in the title with no number stated         -> 5
     "Expert", "10+ Jahre", "sehr langjaehrige"                                          -> 8
   Use null ONLY when the ad says nothing at all about experience level. When both a number
   and wording appear, the number wins.
 - seniority_mismatch: true if the ad wants a senior/lead/head level, is a student/intern
   role, or requires leading/managing people as described above.

Return ONLY this JSON object. No markdown fences, no preamble.
{
  "chosen_cv": "<one of: ${Object.keys(CV_LIBRARY).join(' | ')}>",
  "cv_match_score": <integer 0-100>,
  "assessment": "<at most 25 words: the concrete overlap that makes this a fit, then what is missing. Name specific tools or requirements, not adjectives.>",
  "company_brief": "<at most 10 words: what the company actually does. Empty if the ad does not say.>",
  "new_cv_needed": <true|false>,
  "city": "<city or empty string>",
  "work_mode": "<remote|hybrid|onsite>",
  "de_level": "<native|fluent|very_good|good|basic|mentioned|none>",
  "en_level": "<native|fluent|very_good|good|basic|mentioned|none>",
  "ad_language": "<de|en>",
  "required_years": <integer or null>,
  "seniority_mismatch": <true|false>
}

Write assessment as one sentence a person can act on. Say "Has SQL, Power BI, forecasting;
no dbt or Airflow" — not "good match with some gaps".`;

// --- one ad per call: full attention per JD, and the system prompt above is
// --- byte-identical every time so it is served from the prompt cache.
const BATCH = 1;

const ilanMetni = (j) => `Title: ${j.title || ''}
Company: ${j.company || ''}
Location: ${j.location_raw || ''}
Source: ${j.source || ''}
Salary: ${j.salary_min || ''} - ${j.salary_max || ''}

Description:
${(j.description || '').slice(0, 20000)}`;

const out = [];
for (let s = 0; s < items.length; s += BATCH) {
  const parca = items.slice(s, s + BATCH);
  out.push({
    json: {
      _aiSystem: SYSTEM,
      _aiUserMessage: parca.map((i, k) => `### AD ${k + 1}\n${ilanMetni(i.json)}`).join('\n\n---\n\n'),
      _batch: parca.map(i => i.json),
      _batchCount: parca.length,
      _cvFiles: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(CV_LIBRARY).map(([k,v]) => [k, v.file])),
    }
  });
}
return out;

// Parses one Claude response per ad (BATCH = 1) into one item per ad.
const aiResponses = $input.all();
const prepItems   = $('Prepare AI Scoring Prompt').all();

const VALID_MODE = ['remote', 'hybrid', 'onsite'];
const VALID_LANG = ['en_only', 'en_over_de', 'de_over_en', 'explicit_c1_c2'];
const VALID_LEVEL = ['native','fluent','very_good','good','basic','mentioned','none'];

const sadeLoc = (v) => {
  const s = String(v == null ? '' : v).trim();
  if (!s.startsWith('{')) return s;
  try { const o = JSON.parse(s); return o.locality || o.raw || s; } catch (e) { return s; }
};

const out = [];

aiResponses.forEach((aiItem, bi) => {
  const prep    = prepItems[bi]?.json || {};
  const batch   = Array.isArray(prep._batch) ? prep._batch : [];
  const cvFiles = prep._cvFiles || {};
  const usage   = aiItem.json?.usage || {};

  let aiText = '';
  try { aiText = aiItem.json?.content?.[0]?.text || ''; } catch (e) { aiText = ''; }
  // tolerate a stray ```json fence even though the prompt forbids it
  aiText = aiText.replace(/^\s*```(?:json)?/i, '').replace(/```\s*$/, '').trim();

  let parsed = null;
  try {
    parsed = JSON.parse(aiText);
  } catch (e) {
    const m = aiText.match(/\{[\s\S]*\}/);
    if (m) { try { parsed = JSON.parse(m[0]); } catch (e2) { parsed = null; } }
  }

  const ad = batch[0] || {};
  if (!parsed) {
    out.push({ json: { ...ad, parse_error: true, ai_raw: aiText.slice(0, 500),
                       cv_match_score: 0, _usage: usage } });
    return;
  }

  const key  = String(parsed.chosen_cv || '');
  const file = cvFiles[key] || '';

  out.push({ json: {
    ...ad,
    chosen_cv:          key,
    cv_file:            file,
    cv_unknown:         !file,                       // model named a CV that does not exist
    cv_match_score:     Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Number(parsed.cv_match_score) || 0)),
    new_cv_needed:      parsed.new_cv_needed === true,
    ai_city:            sadeLoc(parsed.city),
    work_mode:          VALID_MODE.includes(parsed.work_mode) ? parsed.work_mode : 'onsite',
    // 2026-08-27: tek birlesik `language_tier` yerine IKI AYRI SEVIYE + ilan dili.
    // Haiku artik SADECE OLGU cikariyor; puanlamayi `Score Location & Language` yapiyor.
    de_level:           VALID_LEVEL.includes(parsed.de_level) ? parsed.de_level : 'none',
    en_level:           VALID_LEVEL.includes(parsed.en_level) ? parsed.en_level : 'none',
    ad_language:        parsed.ad_language === 'en' ? 'en' : 'de',
    required_years:     (() => {                     // 0-40 disi / sayi olmayan -> bilinmiyor
      const y = Math.round(Number(parsed.required_years));
      return Number.isFinite(y) && y > 0 && y <= 40 ? y : null;
    })(),
    seniority_mismatch: parsed.seniority_mismatch === true,
    assessment:         parsed.assessment || '',
    company_brief:      parsed.company_brief || '',
    parse_error:        false,
    _usage:             usage,
  }});
});

const bad = out.filter(o => o.json.parse_error).length;
const unk = out.filter(o => o.json.cv_unknown).length;
console.log(`Parse: ${out.length} ads · parse_error=${bad} · unknown_cv=${unk}`);
return out;

// "Source Down Notice" logic, built & unit-tested OUTSIDE n8n.
// build(src, item) returns the json the Gmail node renders: { subject, html, source, status, category, severity }.
// item = the error-output item json (real shape: { ...date fields, error:{message,name,stack,code,status} }).

function build(src, item) {
  item = item || {};
  const err = item.error || {};

  const esc = (s) => String(s == null ? '' : s)
    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
  const collapse = (s) => String(s == null ? '' : s).replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();

  const rawMsg = String((err && err.message) || item.message || err || 'bilinmeyen hata');

  // --- status code ---
  let status = (typeof err.status === 'number') ? err.status : null;
  if (status == null) { const m = rawMsg.match(/\b([1-5]\d\d)\b/); if (m) status = parseInt(m[1], 10); }
  const code = err.code || null;

  // --- HTML error page detection ---
  const looksHtml = /<!DOCTYPE html|<html[\s>]/i.test(rawMsg);
  let htmlTitle = '';
  if (looksHtml) { const tm = rawMsg.match(/<title>([^<]*)<\/title>/i); if (tm) htmlTitle = collapse(tm[1]); }

  // --- source display + type ---
  const isApify = /apify/i.test(src);
  const nice = String(src || 'Bilinmeyen kaynak').replace(/\s+(HTTP|Apify)$/i, '').trim();
  const kind = isApify ? 'Apify aktörü' : 'HTTP API';
  const whereLook = isApify
    ? 'Apify Console → ilgili aktörün son çalışmasına (run log) bak.'
    : 'Sağlayıcının API/geliştirici paneline bak (kota, anahtar, servis durumu).';

  // --- status label (TR) ---
  const STATUS_TR = { 400: 'Geçersiz istek', 401: 'Yetkilendirme hatası', 403: 'Erişim reddedildi', 404: 'Bulunamadı', 408: 'İstek zaman aşımı', 409: 'Çakışma', 422: 'İşlenemeyen istek', 429: 'Hız sınırı aşıldı', 500: 'Sunucu hatası', 502: 'Hatalı ağ geçidi', 503: 'Servis kullanılamıyor', 504: 'Ağ geçidi zaman aşımı' };
  const statusLabel = status ? (STATUS_TR[status] || 'HTTP hatası') : null;

  // --- category / cause / action / severity ---
  const NETCODES = ['ETIMEDOUT', 'ECONNABORTED', 'ECONNREFUSED', 'ECONNRESET', 'ENOTFOUND', 'EAI_AGAIN', 'ERR_SOCKET', 'ERR_NETWORK'];
  const isNet = (code && NETCODES.some(c => String(code).includes(c))) || /timeout|timed out|socket hang up|network error/i.test(rawMsg);
  let cat, cause, action, sev;
  if (status === 401 || status === 403) {
    cat = 'Kimlik doğrulama'; sev = 'action';
    cause = 'API anahtarı/kimlik bilgisi reddedildi (süresi dolmuş, yanlış ya da kota bitmiş olabilir).';
    action = 'Kimlik bilgisini ve hesabın kotasını kontrol et. ' + whereLook;
  } else if (status === 429) {
    cat = 'Hız sınırı'; sev = 'action';
    cause = 'Çok fazla istek gönderildi, sağlayıcı geçici olarak engelledi.';
    action = 'Tarama sıklığını ya da results_per_page / max_results değerini düşür, sonra tekrar dene.';
  } else if (status && status >= 500) {
    cat = 'Sağlayıcı kesintisi'; sev = 'provider';
    cause = 'Sorun sağlayıcının sunucusunda — senin ayarında bir hata yok.' + (looksHtml ? ' (Standart bir hata sayfası döndürdüler.)' : '');
    action = 'Genelde kendi kendine düzelir. Birkaç gün üst üste sürerse ' + whereLook;
  } else if (status === 400) {
    cat = 'İstek reddedildi'; sev = looksHtml ? 'provider' : 'action';
    cause = looksHtml
      ? 'Sağlayıcı 400 ile birlikte bir HTML hata sayfası döndürdü — çoğunlukla geçici bir kesinti belirtisi, senin ayarında sorun olmayabilir.'
      : 'İstek geçersiz bulundu (parametre ya da endpoint sorunu olabilir).';
    action = looksHtml ? ('Muhtemelen geçici. Sürerse ' + whereLook) : ('Sorgu parametrelerini ve endpoint’i doğrula. ' + whereLook);
  } else if (isNet) {
    cat = 'Ağ / zaman aşımı'; sev = 'provider';
    cause = 'Sağlayıcıya ulaşılamadı ya da yanıt zamanında gelmedi.';
    action = 'Genelde geçici. ' + (isApify ? 'Aktör uzun sürüyorsa timeout değerini artırmayı düşün. ' : '') + whereLook;
  } else {
    cat = 'Bilinmeyen hata'; sev = 'action';
    cause = 'Hata otomatik sınıflandırılamadı; aşağıdaki ham mesaja bak.';
    action = whereLook;
  }

  // --- clean technical detail (never dump provider HTML) ---
  let detail;
  if (looksHtml) detail = 'HTML hata sayfası' + (htmlTitle ? (' — “' + htmlTitle + '”') : '');
  else detail = collapse(rawMsg).slice(0, 240);
  const techBits = [status ? ('HTTP ' + status) : null, code, (err.name && err.name !== 'AxiosError') ? err.name : null].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');

  // --- timestamp (Europe/Berlin) ---
  const whenIso = item.timestamp || new Date().toISOString();
  let whenTxt;
  try { whenTxt = new Date(whenIso).toLocaleString('de-DE', { timeZone: 'Europe/Berlin', dateStyle: 'medium', timeStyle: 'short' }); }
  catch (e) { whenTxt = String(whenIso); }

  // --- subject ---
  const subjTail = status ? ('HTTP ' + status) : (code || 'bağlantı hatası');
  const subject = '⚠️ Job Scanner: ' + nice + ' kaynağı düştü (' + subjTail + ')';

  // --- render ---
  const accent = sev === 'provider' ? '#E67E22' : '#C0392B';
  const statusCell = status ? ('HTTP ' + status + ' — ' + statusLabel) : (code ? esc(code) : 'bağlantı hatası');
  const row = (label, val, top) => '<tr><td style="padding:6px 0;color:#6b7280;width:120px;' + (top ? 'vertical-align:top;' : '') + '">' + label + '</td><td style="padding:6px 0;' + (top ? '' : 'font-weight:600;') + '">' + val + '</td></tr>';

  const html =
    '<div style="font-family:-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:600px;margin:0 auto;color:#1B1F24;">' +
      '<div style="background:' + accent + ';color:#fff;padding:16px 20px;border-radius:10px 10px 0 0;">' +
        '<div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:700;">⚠️ Kaynak arızası: ' + esc(nice) + '</div>' +
        '<div style="font-size:13px;opacity:.9;margin-top:3px;">' + esc(kind) + ' · ' + esc(whenTxt) + '</div>' +
      '</div>' +
      '<div style="border:1px solid #E3E6EA;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 10px 10px;padding:20px;">' +
        '<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;">' +
          row('Durum', statusCell, false) +
          row('Kategori', esc(cat), false) +
          row('Olası neden', esc(cause), true) +
          row('Ne yapmalı', esc(action), true) +
        '</table>' +
        '<div style="margin-top:14px;padding:12px 14px;background:#F5F6F8;border-radius:8px;font-size:12.5px;color:#4b5563;">' +
          '<div style="font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px;">Teknik detay</div>' +
          '<div style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;word-break:break-word;">' + (techBits ? esc(techBits) + ' — ' : '') + esc(detail) + '</div>' +
        '</div>' +
        '<p style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:#16794C;">✔ Tarama diğer kaynaklarla devam etti; bu koşudaki yeni ilanlar yine de kaydedildi.</p>' +
        '<p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b7280;">Aynı kaynak birkaç gün üst üste bu maili gönderirse Sistem Sağlığı sayfasındaki <b>zero_sources</b> sütununu kontrol et — kalıcı bir sorun olabilir.</p>' +
      '</div>' +
      '<div style="text-align:center;color:#9aa1aa;font-size:11px;margin:12px 0;">Sent automatically by your job scanner · n8n</div>' +
    '</div>';

  return { subject, html, source: String(src || ''), status: status, category: cat, severity: sev };
}


